<!--
  Rewordly launcher icon — concept A, "W in a tile".

  Generated geometry, do not hand-edit. The tile and the W both come from
  .workbuddy-ai/logo-work/gen_final.py, which is also what draws the README
  banner, so the launcher icon and the README art cannot drift apart.
  Regenerate there and paste the path data back.

  The W is a six-vertex polyline with a flat-topped centre apex, offset to a
  28-unit stroke band. Every edge sits on an exact 15/75/105 degree angle, so
  the mark stays crisp at 16 dp.

  One even-odd path: the rounded tile is the outer contour and the W is the
  inner one, so the W is a HOLE. The adaptive-icon background is
  @color/brand_primary, which therefore shows through the W — white tile,
  indigo letter, exactly like the concept art.

  108 x 108 is the adaptive-icon viewport and the 66 x 66 safe zone is centred
  on 54, so the 256-unit artwork is scaled by 66/256 and translated by 21.
-->
